[PLAN] feat.compile.tag_permissions: Numeric permissions are tags (design principles 7.2): `#reassociate`, `#contract`, `#approx_math`, `#change_precision`, the four finite-math assumptions and their group `finite_math` are standard tags of the core; `reassociate` and `contract` are the default grants of 7.3, and every other permission is a tag. A permission tag is a fact of the node's permission column, not an attribute. `#strict` (7.4) is a tag of the code: the nodes it marks carry it, and every reader of permissions asks tag::effectivePermissions, which returns the empty set for them -- the default grants included. `std::opt` reassociates a default-permitted sum; under `#strict` the reassociation does not fire, while the exact rewrites (CSE and exact doubling) still may.
