[PLAN] feat.compile.fold_calls: Build-time folding of a call to a pure function with constant arguments (design principles 5.1, 6.5, handover H271): the same evaluator a `when` condition uses reads the body, so a function that computes a field name, an extent or a depth can be called where a compile-time constant is required. A call that does not reduce to one is refused by its own name. Folding happens where a constant is required (a static-access key, a `constas` value); a call in an ordinary value position keeps the ordinary build, so a later pass still sees the program as written.
