[PLAN] feat.modules.array_sum_rounding: A floating-point reduction returns the element type and accumulates in f64, rounding once at the end (design principles 7.3; ruling docs/handover/reviews/reduced-precision.md item (d)). `array::sum` over an f32 array used to accumulate in f32 and round after every addition, so it disagreed with the tensor sum over the same elements, which accumulates in double and rounds once; the two paths now answer the same bits.
